# [Get help]($heading.id('get-help'))

- **Questions and bug reports:** open an issue in the
  [issue tracker](https://github.com/westack-it/sqlz/issues). Include your Zig
  version, the backend and the checker output.
- **Design questions:** the
  [design documents](https://github.com/westack-it/sqlz/tree/main/docs) are
  the specification for 0.1. Most "why does it work this way" questions are
  answered in the
  [architecture decision records](https://github.com/westack-it/sqlz/tree/main/docs/adr).
- **Commercial support:** talk to the [WeStack team](https://westack-it.eu).

# [Contribute]($heading.id('contribute'))

sqlz is open source under the MIT license, and contributions are welcome.

1. Install the pinned toolchain with `mise install` and the git hook with
   `hk install`.
2. For anything larger than a small fix, open an issue first. Check the
   [implementation plan](https://github.com/westack-it/sqlz/blob/main/docs/implementation-plan.md)
   to see what is in progress.
3. Run `mise run ci` before sending a pull request against `main`. It runs the
   offline checks and the full test suite against SQLite and a PostgreSQL 18
   container.

Code follows [`TIGER_STYLE.md`](https://github.com/westack-it/sqlz/blob/main/TIGER_STYLE.md).

# [Code of conduct]($heading.id('code-of-conduct'))

Be kind, assume good intent and keep discussions on topic. Maintainers may
remove content or people that make the community worse for others.
